# Architecture Invariants

Keep these behaviors. Do not "simplify" them away.

## Data & sync (`js/sync.js`, favorites, manage)

- Edits are **local-first** (IndexedDB dirty queue → sync button / daily sync). Do not save straight to GitHub on every edit.
- After sync, clear dirty **only** when the stored record still matches the committed snapshot; **drop** synced local copies so they cannot shadow GitHub.
- Prefer dirty local, else network. Never treat a clean IndexedDB row as permanent source of truth.
- Cook favorites: load pending local or remote `data/favorites.json`. Never auto-stage a stale `localStorage` cook cache for upload on open.
- Catalog delete must check recipe usage and block when referenced (`js/manage.js`).

## Security & a11y

- Escape user/catalog strings in HTML (`CookbookUI.escapeHtml`). Do not add unescaped `innerHTML` for names, ids, or image paths.
- Keep status `role="status"` / `aria-live`, modal focus trap/restore, and loading/`aria-busy` for catalog boot and recipe open.
- Keep ~44px tap targets (`--tap-size`) and global `:focus-visible`.

## Sticky form actions

- In-book `.actions--sticky` must blend with **book page** paper tones. Do not restore the flat white `#fffcf6` slab on `.panel--in-book`.
